@startuml
title POST /api/ai-agents-teams/grants/create/prepare + /send — grantor-signed channel grant
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Grantor\n(team user)" as Grantor #FFD8C2
participant "AgentsTeamsApiSdk\n.createGrant(req)" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "AgentsTeamsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "F1r3node\nchain + observer" as Chain #FFE4A6

Grantor -> SDK : createGrant({grantee, channel,\nchannelPrincipal, agentsTeam, caps,\nauthority, requireToken, minAuth})

group Phase 1 — prepare (deploys nothing)
SDK -> API : POST .../grants/create/prepare
API -> Domain : validate the vocabulary
alt unknown channel / non-delegable command class /\nnon-positive cap / empty principal or grantee
Domain --> API : 422 {code: grant_invalid_request}
API --> SDK : refusal before anything is signed
else legal request
Domain -> Domain : mint grant_id (UUIDv7);\nwhen requireToken: mint 32 CSPRNG bytes,\nhash blake2b-256 -> only the digest enters\nthe contract; render createGrant
Domain --> API : CreateGrantResp { grant_id, contract,\n  issued_at, require_token? }
API --> SDK : PrepareResponse { response, token }
note right of SDK #FFF6C9
The token plaintext appears HERE, exactly
once. It is never stored and cannot be
recovered; surface it immediately.
end note
end
end

group Sign and send
SDK -> SDK : sign the contract locally with the\nGRANTOR's wallet key (secp256k1)
SDK -> API : POST .../grants/create/send\n{ echo, signed contract, token }
API -> Domain : deploy signed createGrant
Domain -> Chain : deploy
note right of Chain #FFF0C7
The clause derives the grantor from the
deploy's signer — never from a parameter —
so a grant can only ever bind its author.
An existing grant_id with identical fields
re-acknowledges; any difference aborts
"grant identity conflict".
end note
alt clause aborts
Chain --> Domain : deploy errored
Domain --> API : 500 {code: internal_error}\n(grant identity conflict)
else clause lands
Chain --> Domain : finalized; acknowledgment true
Domain -> Chain : registration readback: the grant\nmust be observable before the caller\nis told it exists
Domain --> API : deploy id
API --> SDK : 200 SendResp { deployId }
SDK --> Grantor : grant active; channel services\ndiscover it by chain read
end
end
@enduml
